\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Rejoice for a brother deceased,
\par Our loss is his infinite gain;
\par A soul out of prison released,
\par And freed from its bodily chain;
\par With songs let us follow his flight;
\par And mount with his spirit above;
\par Escaped to the mansions of light,
\par And lodged in the Eden of love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our brother the haven hath gained,
\par Out- flying the tempestt and wind,
\par His rest he hath sooner obtained,
\par And left his companions behind,
\par Still tossed on a sea of distress,
\par Hard toiling to make the blest shore,
\par Where all is assurance and peace,
\par And sorrow and sin are no more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. There all the ship's company meet
\par Who sailed with the Saviour beneath,
\par With shouting each other they greet,
\par And triumph o'er trouble and death:
\par The voyage of life's at an end,
\par The mortal affliction is past;
\par The age that in heaven they spend
\par For ever and ever shall last.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

